    {
      "id": "tanzanite",
      "text": "Number ten: a gem. In northern Tanzania, between the city of Arusha and Mount Kilimanjaro, lie the Merelani Hills. This patch of land, about fifty square kilometres, is the only place on Earth where tanzanite is mined. Turn the stone, and it flashes blue, then violet.",
