    },
    {
      "id": "tanzanite-story",
      "text": "It was discovered in nineteen sixty-seven. A year later, the jeweller Tiffany and Company named it tanzanite, after the country, and made it famous. In two thousand two it became a birthstone for December. And more than fifty years on, every natural tanzanite still comes from these same few hills.",
      "scene": {
        "type": "timeline",
        "rank": 10,
        "chapter": "#10 Tanzania: a gem from one hill",
        "events": [
          [
            "1967",
            "Discovered in the Merelani Hills"
