    {
      "id": "axolotl",
      "text": "Number eight lives inside one of the biggest cities on Earth. In the south of Mexico City, the old canals of Xochimilco are the last real wild home of the axolotl, a salamander that looks like it is smiling. Nearby Lake Chalco once had them too, but it is barely usable today.",
