    {
      "id": "calendar-newyear",
      "text": "The Ethiopian year has thirteen months: twelve months of thirty days, plus a tiny thirteenth month, Pagume, of just five or six days. New Year, called Enkutatash, falls on the eleventh of September. And because it counts from a different date for the birth of Christ, it runs about seven years and eight months behind.",
