      "id": "lightning",
      "text": "Number six: a storm that almost never stops. In northwest Venezuela, where the Catatumbo River flows in from Colombia and meets Lake Maracaibo, lightning flashes on up to three hundred nights a year, often for hours. Sailors once called it the Lighthouse of Maracaibo.",
