    {
      "id": "lightning-number",
      "text": "NASA satellites measured it: about two hundred and thirty-three flashes per square kilometre every year, more than anywhere else on the planet. Warm, wet air from the Caribbean meets cool winds from the Andes mountains right above the lake, night after night. It even holds a Guinness World Record.",
