    {
      "id": "hummingbird-scale",
      "text": "A male is about five point seven centimetres long and weighs around one point six grams. That is lighter than a single US dime. It was named for its size: it's barely bigger than a bee. And like other hummingbirds, it hovers in mid-air to drink nectar from flowers.",
