    {
      "id": "darvaza-facts",
      "text": "It's about seventy metres wide and thirty metres deep, fed by natural gas from below. The story goes that it was set alight on purpose, reportedly in nineteen seventy-one, to burn off the gas. In twenty twenty-five, officials said the fire had shrunk more than three times.",
